WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.320
Three questions on the Harappan

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.250
cities. Time to dig in.

3
00:00:05.656 --> 00:00:06.596
Question one.

4
00:00:06.596 --> 00:00:10.116
A large watertight tank, with

5
00:00:10.116 --> 00:00:12.496
steps down at both ends, stood

6
00:00:12.496 --> 00:00:14.006
on this site's citadel.

7
00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:16.436
It is called the Great Bath.

8
00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:18.666
Which site?

9
00:00:19.076 --> 00:00:23.057
Three. Two. One.

10
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:25.857
Mohenjodaro. The tank was made

11
00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:28.417
watertight with bricks set on

12
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.497
edge and a mortar of gypsum.

13
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.977
Scholars think it served some

14
00:00:32.977 --> 00:00:34.047
special purpose.

15
00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:35.897
Question two.

16
00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:38.817
Archaeologists found a field

17
00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:41.417
here, in Rajasthan, with two

18
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.257
sets of furrows at right angles.

19
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:46.137
Two crops, grown together.

20
00:00:46.137 --> 00:00:48.287
Which site?

21
00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:52.806
Three. Two. One.

22
00:00:53.006 --> 00:00:54.766
Kalibangan. Early Harappan

23
00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:58.346
levels. A real field day for

24
00:00:58.346 --> 00:00:59.146
archaeologists.

25
00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:01.825
Question three.

26
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:04.605
A tiny settlement, under seven

27
00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:06.865
hectares, almost entirely given

28
00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:08.165
to craft:

29
00:01:08.165 --> 00:01:11.705
beads, shell, metal, seals and

30
00:01:11.705 --> 00:01:14.215
weights. Which site?

31
00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:18.499
Three. Two. One.

32
00:01:18.699 --> 00:01:20.446
Chanhudaro. Mohenjodaro covered

33
00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.867
a hundred and twenty five

34
00:01:22.867 --> 00:01:26.199
hectares. Chanhudaro was the

35
00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:26.999
workshop.

36
00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.418
For GS1:

37
00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:31.541
Mohenjodaro, the Great Bath.

38
00:01:31.541 --> 00:01:34.301
Kalibangan, the furrowed field.

39
00:01:34.301 --> 00:01:36.248
Chanhudaro, craft production.

40
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:40.011
Three sites, three clues.
